 sections=[
 ["Convert Markdown to PDF online, free","This Markdown to PDF converter renders .md files – READMEs, documentation, notes from Obsidian, Joplin or Typora, and AI-generated answers – into clean, printable PDF documents in your browser. Drop one file or a batch, choose page size, font size, margins and orientation, and download a PDF or ZIP. No upload, no sign-up, no watermark."],
 ["How to convert Markdown to PDF",{"steps":["Drop your .md or .markdown files on the page.","Pick A4, US Letter, Legal or A5, portrait or landscape, and the base font size.","Keep *Page numbers in footer* on for printing.","Press Convert and download the PDF, or a ZIP for several files."]}],
 ["What Markdown is supported?",{"table":[["Element","Syntax","In the PDF"],["Headings","# to ######","Six sizes, rules under H1/H2"],["Bold, italic, code","**b**, *i*, `code`","Bold text and monospace code"],["Lists","- item, 1. item","Bullets and numbers, nested"],["Task lists","- [ ] / - [x]","☐ and ☑ check boxes"],["Tables","| a | b |","Bordered table with header row"],["Code blocks","``` fences","Shaded monospace block, long lines wrapped"],["Block quotes","> quote","Indented with a side bar"],["Horizontal rule","---","Thin divider"],["Links","[text](url)","Blue link text"],["Images","![alt](data:…)","Embedded when given as data URIs; otherwise alt text"]]},"Parsing uses the open-source *marked* library with GitHub-flavoured Markdown enabled, so files written for GitHub or GitLab look the way you expect."],
 ["Why convert Markdown to PDF?",{"list":["Share documentation with people who do not use Markdown editors.","Attach a README, changelog or spec to an e-mail or ticket.","Print lecture notes and study guides written in Obsidian or Notion exports.","Submit assignments written in Markdown as a PDF.","Archive AI chat answers, which are usually Markdown, in a readable format."]}],
 ["Images in Markdown","Images referenced by a local path or a web address cannot be read by a browser tool without uploading or fetching them, so they are shown as their alt text. To include an image, embed it as a data URI – [Image to Base64](/image-to-base64/) creates the exact Markdown snippet – or convert the PDF first and then add pictures with [Add Image to PDF](/add-image-to-pdf/)."],
 ["Unicode, emoji and other scripts","Noto fonts are embedded on demand, so accented letters, Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic, Hebrew, Indic scripts, Thai, Chinese, Japanese and Korean render correctly. Save files as UTF-8, which nearly every Markdown editor does by default."],
 ["Markdown to PDF vs Pandoc and VS Code","Pandoc with LaTeX produces beautiful typesetting but needs a multi-gigabyte install and command-line knowledge; VS Code extensions need a Chromium download. This page needs nothing installed, works on phones and Chromebooks, and converts a batch at once. For plain text with exact line layout use [Text to PDF](/text-to-pdf/); for web pages use [HTML to PDF](/html-to-pdf/)."],
 ["Page setup for documentation","For printed documentation A4 or US Letter at 11 pt with 20 mm margins reads comfortably and matches most corporate templates. Switch to landscape when a document has wide tables or long code samples, and reduce the font size to 9–10 pt if code lines still wrap. Choose A5 for booklets or for reading on a small tablet. Page numbers in the footer help reviewers refer to sections in comments, and each heading starts with extra space so sections are easy to scan. The PDF title is set from the file name, so the tab and the document properties show a meaningful name instead of *Untitled*."],
 ["Tips",{"list":["Leave a blank line before lists and tables – standard Markdown requires it.","Use landscape for wide tables.","Very long code lines are wrapped; reduce font size to keep them on one line.","Merge several converted files with [Merge PDF](/merge-pdf/)."]}],
 ["Privacy",IPRIV]],
 compare=CB([["GitHub-flavoured Markdown","Yes"],["Tables, task lists, code blocks","Yes"],["Batch conversion with ZIP","Yes"],["Page numbers and margins","Yes"],["Works offline","Yes"]]),
